This product follows these parts of multiple-cucumber-html-reporter
(https://github.com/WasiqB/multiple-cucumber-html-reporter), version 4.5.0:

- The information architecture: overview dashboard, feature list, feature page and
  scenario card.
- The scenario status rule: failed, then ambiguous, then undefined, then pending,
  then skipped if any step has that status, otherwise passed.
- The feature status rule, also used here for the run headline: failed, ambiguous or
  undefined if any scenario has that status (in that order); pending only when every
  scenario is pending; skipped only when every scenario is skipped or pending;
  otherwise passed.
- The human-readable duration format ("40ms", "<1ms", "1h 2m 3s", "1d 2h 3m 4s").

One rule differs: a scenario without steps is counted as undefined, as Godog counts
it, where multiple-cucumber-html-reporter leaves it out of the counts.

No source code, templates, styles, scripts, images or fonts from that project are
included. The templates, CSS, JavaScript and SVG charts in this repository were
written for it. No fragment has been copied; if one is ever copied, its source file
and line range will be listed here.

